#% if ha_mcp_url %#
---
#| jgct#237, jg-base#221/#232: Secret `ha-im-token` in `claudecode`, key
   `token`. jg-base mounts the whole Secret at /etc/ha-mcp on im's app
   container (optional, 0400) and sets HA_MCP_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/ha-mcp/token.
   Here, under cluster-tenants, because the URL it pairs with exists only when
   an app_repos entry runs HA -- so this directory is always rendered when it
   is -- and because cluster-tenants already applies im-apps-write-key into the
   same namespace after cluster-apps-base. Like that key, an im already running
   when this first appears does not see it: restart im after the first apply. #|
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: ha-im-token
  namespace: claudecode
stringData:
  token: #{ ha_im_token | trim | tojson }#
#% endif %#
